## ⚡ Quick Reference (Critical Rules Only)

### Control Signal Priority
```
reset > clock_enable > enable
```
- **Reset**: Forces safe state (highest priority)
- **Clock Enable**: Freezes sequential logic when low
- **Functional Enable**: Gates functional work

### Tiered Rule System
- **Tier 1** (Strict RTL): `common/`, `core/`, `top/` - Verilog portability required
- **Tier 2** (Relaxed Data): `datadef/` - Records allowed, document conversion
- **Tier 3** (Full VHDL-2008): `tb/` - No constraints (testing only)

### Direct Instantiation (MANDATORY for Top Layer)
```vhdl
-- ✅ REQUIRED
U1: entity WORK.module_name port map (...);

-- ❌ FORBIDDEN
component module_name is ... end component;
```

### Signal Naming
- `ctrl_*` - Control signals
- `cfg_*` - Configuration parameters
- `stat_*` - Status and monitoring

### Status Register Bits
- **Bit 7**: FAULT (sticky, cleared only on reset)
- **Bit 6**: ALARM (sticky, cleared only on reset)
- **Bits 5-0**: Module-specific (state, flags, etc.)

